{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>And he called his name Zeraḥ.</b> Zeraḥ after the sun (חמה), Peretz after the moon (לבנה), and the kingship of the House of David comes from Peretz, who corresponds to the moon. And it is known that the days of the moon are 29 days, and therefore you will find from Peretz son of Judah to Zedekiah, 29 men. How so: Peretz, Hezron, Ram, Aminadav, Naḥshon, Salmah, Boaz, Oved, Yishai, David — so David is tenth from Peretz. From David to Yehoyakhin you will find 19 kings, all of them a king son of a king, and they are: Shelomo, Reḥav'am, Aviyah, Asa, Yehoshaphat, Yehoram, Aḥazyahu, Yoash, Amatz'yah, Uziyahu, Yotam, Aḥaz, Yeḥezkiyah, Menasheh, Amon, Yoshiyahu, Yeho'aḥaz, Yehoyakim, Yehoyakhin, Zedekiah. They are 29 men corresponding to the days of the moon. And just as the moon sets after 29 days, so the kingship of the House of David was cut off and the Temple was destroyed in the days of Zedekiah, who is the 29th from Peretz." "<b>But</b> in the Midrash, Shemot Rabbah arranged this reckoning in a different manner: that the days of the moon are joined by addition and subtraction corresponding to the kings of Judah, among whom there were those whose kingdom grew strong corresponding to the days of addition, and those whose strength failed corresponding to the days of diminution until the kingdom ceased entirely, just as happens to the moon, which waxes and afterward wanes until it sets completely. And this is what they expounded (Exodus 12:2): ״החדש הזה לכם״ — before the Holy One, blessed be He, brought Israel out of Egypt, He informed them that the kingdom would not endure for them except thirty generations, as it is said ״החדש הזה לכם״ — the moon is thirty days and their kingdom is thirty generations. The moon begins to shine on the first day of the month, and it goes on shining more and more until the fifteenth day, when its disk (דיסקוס) is filled, and from the fifteenth onward it diminishes, and on the thirtieth it is not seen. So too Israel: from Abraham to Shelomo, fifteen generations. Abraham began to shine, as it is said (Isaiah 41:2): ״מי האיר ממזרח צדק״ and so forth. And likewise it says (Isaiah 42:6): ״אני ה׳ קראתיך״ and so forth. Yitzḥak came and he too shone, as it is said ״ויזרע יצחק״, and it is written (Psalms 97:11): ״אור זרוע לצדיק״. Ya'akov came and added light, as it is said (Isaiah 10:17): ״והיה אור ישראל לאש״, and afterward: Yehudah, Peretz, Hezron, Ram, Aminadav, Naḥshon, Salmah, Boaz, Oved, Yishai, David. Once Shelomo came, the moon's disk was filled, as it is said (I Chronicles 29:23): ״וישב שלמה על כסא ה׳ למלך״ — on the throne of the Holy One, blessed be He. What is written of His throne? (Ezekiel 1:10): ״ודמות פניהם פני אדם ופני אריה״. Of Shelomo it is written (I Kings 7:29): ״ועל המסגרות אשר בין השלבים אריות״, and it is written there: ״ומעשה האופנים כמעשה אופן המרכבה״. On the throne of the Holy One, blessed be He, no evil thing touches, as it is said (Psalms 5:5): ״לא יגורך רע״, and of Shelomo it is written (I Kings 5:18): ״אין שטן ואין פגע רע״ and so forth. The Holy One, blessed be He, made six heavens and He is in the seventh, and of Shelomo's throne it is written (I Kings 5:18): ״שש מעלות לכסא״, and he sits on the seventh step — see, the moon's disk was filled. And from Shelomo onward the kings began to wane and diminish: Reḥav'am, Aviyah, and so all of them up to Zedekiah. Once Zedekiah came (II Kings 25:7): ״ואת עיני צדקיהו עור״ — the light of the moon was extinguished. And all those years, even though Israel sinned, the patriarchs would pray for them and make peace between Israel and their Father in heaven, as it is said (Psalms 72:3): ״ישאו הרים שלום לעם״, and 'mountains' means the patriarchs, as it is said (Micah 6:2): ״שמעו הרים את ריב ה׳ והאיתנים מוסדי ארץ״, as it is written (Psalms 72:7): ״ורוב שלום עד בלי ירח״ — until the moon set and the Temple was destroyed at the thirtieth generation. End quote." "<b>You thus</b> learn: from Abraham to Shelomo, fifteen generations, for King David was the fourteenth from Abraham, and likewise דו\"ד (David) equals 14, and Shelomo his son was the fifteenth from Abraham, corresponding to the completion of the moon's filling, and likewise Zedekiah was the fifteenth from Shelomo — except that Shelomo corresponds to the filling of the moon and Zedekiah to its setting. And it is known that most of the kings were idolaters, until Zedekiah came, who was the last king to reign after Yehoyakhin, and he too did evil like them; and he was not the son of Yehoyakhin. And then the moon set — the Temple was destroyed in his days through Nevukhadnetzar. As it is written in Jeremiah (Jeremiah 39): 'In the ninth year of Zedekiah king of Judah, in the tenth month, Nevukhadra'tzar king of Babylon came with all his army against Jerusalem and besieged it.' And it is written there: 'In the eleventh year of Zedekiah, in the fourth month, on the ninth of the month, the city was breached.' And it is written there: 'And in the fifth month, on the tenth of the month — that being the nineteenth year of King Nevukhadra'tzar — Nevuzaradan the chief executioner came and burned the house of HaShem and the house of the king,' and so forth. And our Rabbis of blessed memory expounded in tractate Horayot, chapter Kohen Mashiaḥ: 'This is Shalom, this is Zedekiah. Why was his name called Shalom? Because the kingdom of the House of David was completed (נשלמה) in his days. And what was his name? Mattanyah was his name, as it is said (II Kings 24): ״וימלך מלך בבל את מתניה דודו תחתיו ויסב את שמו צדקיהו״ — and why was his name called Zedekiah? He said to him: You must justify (תצדיק) the judgment upon yourself if you rebel against me.' And it is written (II Chronicles 36): ״וגם במלך נבוכדנאצר מרד אשר השביעו באלהים״ and so forth." "<b>And by way of</b> the Kabbalah: in this verse, in these two infants, there is a great secret concerning the mystery of the kingship of the House of David. I shall reveal to you a little of its hidden depths; incline your ear and hear." "<b>It is known</b> that the name Elohim mentioned in Genesis is King of the Universe, and it is the answer — and this is what we say on Rosh HaShanah: on it the world was created, 'the holy King' and 'the King of judgment,' for that day is the beginning of His works, since there is no king without a people. And Scripture said (Genesis 1): ״ויאמר אלהים יהי אור ויהי אור״ — to make known that from the force of the kingdom of heaven called Elohim, these two lights were emanated; and therefore it says ״ויהי אור״ (and there was light), in the singular, and it did not say so concerning the rest of the work of creation. And you should reflect that the intention is not that there were literally two lights, but that there were two forces within it: one a masculine force and the second a feminine force. But the first light was only one — and it is one embracing masculine force and feminine force — and from this light the sun (חמה) and moon (לבנה) were emanated on the fourth day, as I explained there in the section of Genesis, and the masculine force was emanated upon the sun and the feminine force upon the moon." "<b>And from now</b> contemplate the matter of Judah and Tamar and these two children, Perez and Zerah; from it the matter of the work of Creation will become clear to you. And this is what our Rabbis, of blessed memory, said: 'The kingdom on earth is like the kingdom of the firmament.' Behold, Judah was called by this name on account of the confession (hoda'ah), as Leah said (Genesis 29:35): ״הפעם אודה את ה׳״ — 'This time I will praise HaShem.' And he is the fourth among the tribes, and the special Name is inscribed upon him, and he was king and head of the kingdom of the House of David. Therefore Tamar was worthy to mate with Judah to perform that act, because her name was Tamar, which embraces the power of maleness and the power of femaleness — for the lulav is the male and its fruit is the date (tamar), which is male on the outside and in its seed inside it is female, something you will not find in any other trees. And Perez and Zerah were worthy to be emanated from Tamar, for they correspond to the sun and the moon, which are emanated from the first light that embraces male and female. For Zerah corresponds to the sun, which shines constantly in equal fashion, and Perez corresponds to the moon, which is sometimes full, sometimes lacking and breached (הנפרצת). Therefore the kingdom of the House of David, which comes from Perez, is obliged to be at certain times established and at certain times nullified." "<b>And if</b> you gain insight into the verse, you will find that just as the sun is matched with the moon, so Zerah and Perez were matched in one womb, and matched in the firstborn status. For Zerah was the firstborn in the giving of the hand — as it is written, ״ויתן יד״ — and it says of him, ״זה יצא ראשונה״, and it also says, ״ויהי כמשיב ידו״ — and it did not say וישב ידו. And Perez was the firstborn in his departure from the womb, and from this it says, ״ואחר יצא אחיו אשר על ידו השני״ — for Zerah was the last in the first opening of the womb, even though he was first in the giving of the hand. And know that the complete firstborn of the two was Perez, who was the first to depart from the womb, for the Holy One, blessed be He, designated the firstborn by the first opening of the womb, and so the verse mentions his name first. And from this you will find concerning the kingdom of the House of David (Psalms 89:28): ״אף אני בכור אתנהו עליון למלכי ארץ״. And since the kingdom of the House of David comes from Perez, and Perez corresponds to the moon, the Masters of Truth mentioned it in connection with the renewal of the moon, and they sent as its sign: דוד מלך ישראל חי וקיים. And this statement, according to its plain sense, means that the moon was called by the name David because David comes from Perez, who corresponds to the moon, and also because the moon is called the lesser light (המאור הקטן). And it is written of David (I Samuel 17): ״ודוד הוא הקטן״. And in saying חי וקיים, his intent is to say that the moon is visible." "<b>And by way of the secret (sod),</b> which is where we are, this statement alludes to the power of the moon, which they called 'David king of Israel' in the language of Knesset Israel. And therefore he mentioned חי וקיים — this is what is alluded to us in the inner meaning of their words (Daniel 7:9): ״עד די כרסון רמיו״ — two thrones. And in the chapter 'Ein dorshin' in tractate Ḥagigah, our Sages revealed their understanding in this matter: some say one for Him and one for David; some say one for righteousness (tzedakah) and one for justice (din); some say one for a throne and one for a footstool — a throne to sit upon and a footstool to rest His feet upon. And the Sages appear to disagree, but it is not so; rather they all concur in one view, and all is one matter and one root. And this is what is written (Hosea 3:5): ״ובקשו את ה׳ אלהיהם ואת דויד מלכם״ — this is Knesset Israel. And concerning this power, our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded: Israel were worthy that they should never be exiled from their place, and the decree was not issued until they denied the kingdom of Heaven and the kingdom of the House of David, as it is said (II Samuel 20:1): ״אין לנו חלק בדוד ולא נחלה בבן ישי איש לאהליו ישראל״. And you should reflect on the fact that the verse does not duplicate the language, as the Masters of the Peshat think; rather the matter is that they denied the kingdom above and also denied the kingdom of the son of Jesse below, and they served idolatry, for concerning this they said איש לאהליו, and our Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded איש לאלהיו — 'each man to his god.' And this is clear." "<b>And the verse</b> mentions four times the word יד in connection with Zerah: ״ויתן יד״, ״ותקשר על ידו״ שני, ״ויהי כמשיב ידו״, ״אשר על ידו השני״. And they correspond to four bans (ḥaramim) in which Achan son of Zerah stretched out his hand. And they are: the ban of Amalek, the ban of Sihon and Og, the ban of the Canaanites, the ban of Jericho."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {2 "Horayot reference: chapter heading is לפני פרוס הפסח in standard editions; he cites by an alternate or internal chapter title.", 7 "The method header reads ע\"ד הסוד, a variant of the four standard method labels in Rabbeinu Bahya's system; rendered literally as 'by way of the secret (sod).'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:19:28.711626680Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}